+        # /rtx/descriptorSets defaults to 10000 (registered in libgpu.foundation.plugin.so) and is
+        # the max descriptor-set count handed to createDescriptorPool. Multi-scene vector envs blow
+        # through it: descriptor sets scale as (render products x RTX passes x frames-in-flight), so
+        # at 3 cameras per scene, ~10 scenes crosses 10000 and allocation fails with
+        #     [gpu.foundation.plugin] Unable to allocate descriptor sets.
+        #     [rtx.denoising.plugin] Failed to allocate ParameterBlock resources.
+        # which Isaac turns into a segfault DURING scene load -- with GPU memory nearly empty
+        # (17 GB of 46 GB used), because a descriptor pool is a fixed-count arena, not a heap.
+        #
+        # 360000 / 900000 are the values NVIDIA itself passes in 71 extension.toml files in this
+        # install (e.g. isaacsim.core.api/config/extension.toml) -- but only inside [[test]] blocks,
+        # so nothing sets them at normal app launch and OmniGibson runs on the bare default.
+        # reservedDescriptors is clamped against a queried device limit, so it degrades gracefully.
+        #
+        # These are read once during RTX ResourceManager init, so they MUST be set before startup:
+        # carb.settings and app.set_setting() are post-launch and have no effect on them.
+        sys.argv.append("--/rtx/descriptorSets=360000")
+        sys.argv.append("--/rtx/reservedDescriptors=900000")
